Canonical JSON: 
```dart
static String canonicalJson(Map<String, Object> data) {
  final copy = <String, Object>{};
  data.forEach((k,v){ if (k == 'exportedAt') return; if (v is List) { final rows = v.map((e)=> e is Map ? Map<String,Object?>.from(e) : {'value': e}).toList(); rows.sort((a,b) => _rowKey(a).compareTo(_rowKey(b))); copy[k]=rows; } else copy[k]=v; });
  final keys = copy.keys.toList()..sort();
  return jsonEncode({for (final k in keys) k: copy[k]});
}
```
_rowKey: if id present use id padded else jsonEncode row. Simpler: `jsonEncode(row)` sorting handles determinism for id ordering too, though rows sorted lexicographically by JSON (id numbers string 10 < 9 lexicographically) — but that's deterministic for same data. Sorting by id preferred: use `(row['id'] ?? 0)` numeric then JSON string fallback.

