Core algorithm:

```dart
class AutoBackup {
  static String fileNameFor(DateTime t) => 'gongzhuriji_${DateFormat('yyyy-MM-dd_HHmm').format(t)}.wrdx';

  static Duration delayUntilNext3(DateTime now) {
    var next = DateTime(now.year, now.month, now.day, 3);
    if (!next.isAfter(now)) next = next.add(const Duration(days: 1));
    return next.difference(now);
  }

  static Future<String> fingerprint(String tablesJson, List<ImageMeta> images) async {
    // strip exportedAt
    final sb = StringBuffer();
    sb.write(_canonicalJson(jsonDecode(tablesJson)));  // or just take json string minus exportedAt
    images.sort(by name);
    for (final i in images) sb.write('\n${i.name}\t${i.size}\t${i.modifiedMs}');
    return sha256Hex(utf8.encode(sb.toString()));
  }
```
For canonicalization: `exportTables()` returns Map with 'exportedAt' varying. Remove key then jsonEncode with sorted keys. I'll write a `stableJson(Object?)` that recursively sorts map keys. That also makes DB row order stable (query order is by rowid — stable enough).

Actually the spec says "对 exportTables() 的 JSON ... 算 sha256". Removing exportedAt is essential. I'll document.

